                                                "sense_id": "0e975ec2-f147-36ce-9f66-390d4fd25bed",
                                                "text": "If the afternoon was fine they strolled together in the park, very slowly, and with pauses to draw breath wherever the ground sloped upward. The slightest effort made the patient cough."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3bb3a31f-3424-4768-ad9d-4b3192eab561",
                                                "sense_id": "0e975ec2-f147-36ce-9f66-390d4fd25bed",
                                                "text": "St. Lawrence Station is very prettily situated, high cliffs on the left, and the lush vegetation of the Undercliff sloping down to the sea on the right."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "234f158c-43dc-3ca2-bf3f-399a941f2c02",
                                        "entry_id": "f316381c-6369-3fac-9260-1597a9df4c68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To form with a slope; to give an oblique or slanting direction to; to incline or slant."
